  "article_notes": "Zagreb university clinic, 35 B. canis dogs (PCR; part of the Beck et al. 2009 cohort) and 14 healthy controls. Samples on the day of admission; imidocarb was given subcutaneously on the day of admission, order not stated. Superscripts marking complicated vs uncomplicated significance in Tables 1 and 3 were partly lost in PDF conversion; significance taken from the Results text, which lists PLT (Table 1) and BUN, creatinine, bilirubin, ALT, AP and GGT (Table 3). Mortality 4/7 complicated dogs, but no marker compared by survival. Infected vs healthy comparisons (Tables 1, 2, 4) not extracted.",
  "skipped_infected_vs_healthy": 15,
  "severity_definitions": [
    {
      "key": "S1",
      "outcome_class": "complicated",
      "label": "complicated vs uncomplicated babesiosis",
      "definition": "Complicated if one or more of: renal dysfunction (creatinine > 180 umol/l), hepatic dysfunction (ALT > 176 IU/l and AP > 360 IU/l, or bilirubin > 100 umol/l), respiratory dysfunction (radiographic pulmonary oedema or dyspnoea), muscular involvement (CPK > 600 IU/l). Complications seen: renal 5/7, hepatic 3/7, muscular 2/7, ARDS 1/7; 4 of 7 complicated dogs died.",
      "severe_group": "complicated (n=7)",
      "comparison_group": "uncomplicated (n=28)",
      "quote": "On the basis of clinical manifestations and laboratory data the affected dogs were divided into two groups: complicated (Group 1.1.) and uncomplicated (Group 1.2.) babesiosis (Jacobson and Clark, 1994).",
      "components": [
        "renal",
        "hepatic or icterus",
        "pulmonary",
        "rhabdomyolysis"
      ],
      "euthanasia_included": "not applicable",
      "definition_source": "Jacobson and Clark 1994 complications; bilirubin criterion from Weiser 1992 / Matijatko et al. 2009",
      "follow_up_horizon": null
    },
    {
      "key": "S2",
      "outcome_class": "anaemia_grade",
      "label": "severe vs moderate vs mild anaemia (uncomplicated dogs only)",
      "definition": "Uncomplicated dogs graded by haematocrit: severe HCT < 16 (n=1), moderate 16 <= HCT < 35 (n=9), mild HCT >= 35 (n=18).",
      "severe_group": "moderate anaemia (n=9); severe n=1 not analysed",
      "comparison_group": "mild anaemia (n=18)",
      "quote": "Furthermore, depending on the severity of anaemia, dogs with uncomplicated babesiosis were classified as suffering from severe (haematocrit (HCT) < 16; Group 1.2.1.), moderate (16 ≤ HCT < 35; Group 1.2.2.), or mild disease (HCT ≥ 35; Group 1.2.3.) (Jacobson and Clark, 1994).",
      "components": [
        "anaemia grade"
      ],
      "euthanasia_included": "not applicable",
      "definition_source": "Jacobson and Clark 1994",
      "follow_up_horizon": null
    }
